      "citation_count": 135,
      "cited_by_count": 135,
      "is_oa": true,
      "oa_status": "diamond",
      "abstract": "Our aim in this research is to investigate the motion of a beam on an internally bent nanowire by using the fractional calculus theory.To this end, we first formulate the classical Lagrangian which is followed by the classical Euler-Lagrange equation.Then, after introducing the generalized fractional Lagrangian, the fractional Euler-Lagrange equation is provided for the motion of the considered beam on the nanowire.An efficient numerical scheme is introduced for implementation and the simulation results are reported for different fractional-order values and various initial settings.These results indicate that the fractional responses approach the classical ones as the fractional order goes to unity.In addition, the fractional Euler-Lagrange equation provides a flexible model possessing more information than the classical description -the fact that leads to a considerably better evaluation of the hidden features of the real system under investigation.",
